<h1>A. Merritt's Fantasy Magazine Listings</h1>

From <I>Tuck's Encyclopedia of Science Fiction and Fantasy</I>:
<p>
<pre>
    This magazine was started because of interest in Abraham
    Merritt's fiction; most issues featured one of his stories.
    The never-published 6th issue was to have had "The Snake Mother,"
    A. Merritt, and "The Lost Garden," M. Brand [F. Faust].
</pre>
<p>
Concerning the Canadian Edition:
<p>
<pre>
    Entire contents, covers and dates are identical with the US
    editions, except that the magazines are a half inch longer,
    enabling the panel at the bottom of the front cover to give
    the title of the secondary story as well as the main novel.
    Advertisements are the same as the US except that two Canadian
    beer firms have the outside back covers.
</pre>
